off the grid, while Hill jumped into second behind him.","q":true,"src":"Wikipedia","c":0},{"lap":11,"text":"Gurney got by Brabham and Ginther and briefly took third place, but on lap 11, Ginther retook the spot behind his teammate when Gurney slid half off the track, inches from the Armco, on a patch of oil in the Loop.","q":true,"src":"Wikipedia","c":4},{"lap":12,"text":"On lap 12, the two leaders were already coming up to lap the tail-enders. When Clark was delayed in the traffic, Hill took the lead away from him.","q":true,"src":"Wikipedia","c":1},{"lap":19,"text":"By lap 19, however, Clark had lowered the lap record to 1:15.4, well under his qualifying time, and retaken the lead for good.","q":true,"src":"Wikipedia","c":0},{"lap":69,"text":"Brabham closed the gap between them, and when he grabbed fourth place from the American on lap 69, he claimed the first Championship points ever scored by the Brabham make.","q":true,"src":"Wikipedia","c":3},{"lap":100,"text":"Clark eventually clocked a 1:15.0 on lap 70 for the fastest lap of the race, and eased off from his biggest lead of 17 seconds to take the second consecutive American Grand Prix win for Team Lotus.","q":true,"src":"Wikipedia","c":0},{"lap":100,"text":"Indeed, moments after the Scot had taken the checkered flag, a drizzle began to fall.","q":true,"src":"Wikipedia","c":0}],"x":{"drivers":[{"id":470,"ref":"mayer","name":"Timmy Mayer","code":null,"nationality":"American","dob":"1938-02-22","helmet":null,"seasons":{"1962":{"car":"cooper-climax_1962","source":"history","skills":{"pace":[0.9414,0.4604],"quali":[0.7618,0.3336]}}}}],"cars":[{"id":"brabham_1962","ref":"brabham","name":"Brabham","year":1962,"pace":-1.518,"pace_sd":0.5,"deg_rel":0.0,"n_races":3,"p_mech_lap":0.00758,"colours":null,"source":"history"}]}}